  "text": "For laboratory analysis, 2 ml of venous blood was collected from each participant after obtaining informed consent from the caregiver and assent from the child. The venipuncture site was disinfected with an alcohol swab, and blood was drawn into EDTA-containing vacutainers to prevent clotting. Complete blood count (CBC) was performed using an automated Coulter counter, which measured hemoglobin concentration, red blood cell indices (MCV, MCH, MCHC), packed cell volume, red cell distribution width, white blood cell count, and platelet count."
